# Every pull request needs a review from the repository lead, on every path. Without this file the
# ruleset's "require code owner review" has nothing to require and lets any approval through.
#
# GitHub never counts an author's approval of their own pull request, so the lead's own pull requests
# cannot satisfy this rule. They are merged through the admin bypass, which is scoped to pull requests
# only: even the lead cannot push to main or develop.
